**Michael Jordan scores 32/100 — PASS. He is not an Emerging Entity Gap, and the packet saying so (plus the one winnable lane if the pipeline drafts him anyway) is saved at `docs/content-analysis/entity-gaps/Michael-Jordan.md`.**

What the audit found:

- **The SERP is the strongest that exists.** Personal Wikipedia page, Britannica, the Naismith Hall of Fame, IMDb, and EBSCO all hold dedicated biographies; every fact query (age 63, wife Yvette Prieto, parents, height) has an authoritative instant answer. That triggers the full -20 penalty on a 52-point subtotal. There is no world where 9takes becomes the biography of record here.
- **Demand is huge but perennial, not rising faster than coverage.** Two genuine catalysts exist — his NBA on NBC "special contributor" role with the recurring "MJ: Insights to Excellence" segment (2025-26 season, still generating coverage as of August 11), and the 23XI Racing antitrust settlement (dismissed February 2026) followed by Tyler Reddick's historic season start. They add news volume to a fully served name; they don't open a gap.
- **The one weak sub-SERP is personality intent.** `michael jordan personality type enneagram` returns personality-database, Boo, and JobCannon-tier thin sites — and two of the top hits are actually **Michael B. Jordan** pages. The personality SERP is confused about which Jordan is being asked about, which matters because 9takes already publishes a Michael B. Jordan profile. That's both the site's biggest cannibalization risk and its clearest edge: a page that locks the entity in the first hundred words beats every directory that can't.

Since the backlog queues him anyway ("evergreen GOAT search volume"), the packet gives the pipeline its constraints rather than just a rejection: target personality intent exclusively (consensus typing elsewhere is 3w4), concede all biography queries, cross-link both Jordan pages for disambiguation, and organize the piece around the manufactured-grievance contradiction — the most image-controlled athlete ever, running on invented slights from the Hall of Fame speech to "the lawsuit was personal" at 63. Source depth is a trivial pass (The Last Dance, the 2009 HOF speech, Lazenby, Halberstam, adversarial teammate testimony). Claims-to-avoid section covers the 1993 gambling-suspension conspiracy, clinical language, and tabloid marriage material.

